id: pm-gh1695
title: "GH-1695: accept settings paths and provide bounded config-key recovery"
description: "Canonical intake for https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/issues/1695. Implement the reported SDK and CLI recovery contract after current-source reproduction, preserving deterministic validation, privacy and no-write refusal behavior."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 2
tags[4]: agent-ux,config,"gh:1695",sdk
created_at: "2026-11-09T07:32:05.563Z"
updated_at: "2026-11-09T16:33:00.607Z"
closed_at: "2026-11-09T16:32:59.789Z"
completed_at: "2026-11-09T16:32:59.789Z"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 90
acceptance_criteria: Accept every supported settings path as an alias in SDK-backed config get/set without bypassing validation; Unknown keys offer at most three nearest legal keys and a working config-list inspection command; Preserve complete legal keys in structured recovery and reject unknown keys without settings writes
parent: pm-8jdc
risk: medium
confidence: high
resolution: Validated dotted settings aliases and scalar context leaves; bounded key suggestions with complete SDK domains; executable tracker-scoped JSON inventory preserving extension isolation; exact independent inventory coverage and an explicit missing-refusal guard in the shell replay.
expected_result: "Supported configuration paths round-trip safely, inspection stays in the selected tracker, inventory coverage remains exact, and absent SDK refusals fail clearly without undefined property access."
actual_result: "All three linked test commands pass after the DeepScan repair; the two-tracker replay retains selected 11 versus ambient 22 and all 60 independently expected inventory leaves. The thirteen-file instrumented source cohort previously passed 356 tests; no runtime source, API signature, analyzer settings, performance budget or coverage threshold changed in this test-only follow-up. Next-head hosted DeepScan and complete CI admission remain required."
